  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinPhys 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You are currently recruiting patients to participate in a Phase II clinical
    trial. A patient is interested in joining the study, but they do not meet the
    eligibility criteria.\n\n<b>It is the physician\u2019s responsibility to ensure
    that only eligible patients who can safely participate are enrolled in a clinical
    trial.</b>\n\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: Physicians help decide who can safely take part in a clinical trial
    by carefully reviewing eligibility guidelines. These guidelines look at things
    like overall health, other medical conditions, and past treatments to help protect
    patients and ensure the study results are meaningful. Even when someone is eager
    to participate, enrolling them when there are known risks could put their health
    at risk and make it harder to understand whether the treatment truly works.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Clinical
